data.content:
Build passes ✅. Here's a summary of all breaking changes and fixes:

---

### Breaking changes fixed in this project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix Applied |
|---|----------------|-------------|
| 1 | **TFM & packages** | `net8.0` → `net9.0`; packages `8.0.0` → `9.0.0` |
| 2 | **`HasData` with `DateTime.UtcNow`** — EF Core 9 throws "pending model changes" because the value changes every evaluation | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024, 1, 1, ...)` |
| 3 | **`Migrate()` inside explicit transaction** — EF Core 9 now manages its own transactions and throws if wrapped | Removed `CreateExecutionStrategy` + `BeginTransaction` wrapper; call `Migrate()` directly |
| 4 | **Design package not found (SDK ≥ 9.0.200)** — `PrivateAssets="all"` omits it from `.deps.json` | Added `<Publish>true</Publish>` and explicit `<IncludeAssets>` |

### Cosmos DB project fixes (your separate project)

You mentioned a separate Cosmos DB project with existing documents. Apply these three fixes there:

**5. Discriminator renamed to `$type`** — existing documents use `"Discriminator"`:
```csharp
// Preserve old property name for existing documents
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");
```

**6. `id` no longer contains discriminator** — existing docs have `"EntityType|Key"` format:
```csharp
// Preserve old compound id format so existing docs remain accessible
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

**7. Sync I/O now throws** — replace all synchronous Cosmos queries:
```csharp
// BREAKS:  db.SaveChanges();       →  await db.SaveChangesAsync();
// BREAKS:  query.ToList();         →  await query.ToListAsync();
// BREAKS:  query.FirstOrDefault(); →  await query.FirstOrDefaultAsync();
```
